  Properties matched to the donor's own measured shape (item §2, live def
  dump this item cites): the deep liquid is Impassable, avoidWander,
  waterBodyType None (propane is not recognised as drinkable water by DBH or
  anything else — matches "propane, not water"); the frozen margin crust is
  Standable at a low pathCost, also waterBodyType None (it is not liquid).
  Parented on WaterDeepBase / WaterShallowBase — confirmed to carry a real
  Name="..." attribute by direct read (Core/Defs/TerrainDefs/Terrain_Water.xml,
  same citation RUT_ScaldWater.xml's own header already gives), unlike
  Lake/Ocean.

  Texture: reuses vanilla's own WaterDeepRamp/WaterShallowRamp paths, the
  same convention RUT_ScaldWater.xml already established for this mod family
  (no donor mod dependency, no new art needed — this is ordinary vanilla
  texture reuse, not a placeholder for a missing donor asset). A dedicated
  "frozen propane crust" look is real, owed art work, not done here.

  ✅ RE-CHECKED under LIQUID_TERRAIN_AUTHORED_TWICE_1 (closed 2026-09-27):
  RM_TheChillDeep/RM_SolidPropane (this file) both share the words
  "liquid propane" with FlowWorks' RM_PropaneShallow/Deep but are not a fork
  of the same content — RM_TheChill.xml uses BOTH at once, deliberately,
  for two different depths of the same lake (this file's pair as the main
  waterDeepTerrain/waterShallowTerrain, FlowWorks' pair as the fishable
  <coastal> shore edge — see RM_TheChill.xml's own SEA_FLOOR_AND_CATCH_
  PASS_1 comment). Neither carries a burn/damage number the other
  contradicts, so nothing here needed folding into the generator or
  deleting.

  ✅ RE-CHECKED AGAIN under TERMINALBIOMES_LIQUID_RETARGET_1 (Q7 ownership
  ruling execution, 2026-09-28): same conclusion holds. RM_TheChillDeep/
  RM_SolidPropane are the lake's own MAIN BODY terrain (waterDeepTerrain/
  waterShallowTerrain on RM_TheChill.xml) and FlowWorks' RM_PropaneDeep/
  RM_PropaneShallow are already directly wired as that same BiomeDef's
  <coastal> shore-fishing edge — both in active, deliberate, simultaneous
  use on one BiomeDef, not a stale fork. There is nothing generic left to
  retarget here: this pair is a keeper, not a duplicate. Do not re-open this
  a third time on a defName-similarity read alone.
